1. e4 { What move kickstarts the Caro-Kann? } 1... c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. Nf3 { 4.Nf3 is the most popular move after 3.exd5 exd5. How should Black respond? } 4... Nc6 (4... Nf6 { This move is an alternative move and is just as good, but not what I'm looking for. }) 5. Bb5?! { Bb5 is the most common move in this position. However, this move is an inaccuracy. How can you exploit it with a forcing move? } 5... Qa5+ 6. Nc3 { Black is almost already equal in this position. Find the best continuation. } 6... Bg4 (6... e6 { This is the second best move, but it blocks in your light-squared bishop. }) 7. Bxc6+ bxc6 8. O-O { Castling is played 45% of the time in this position. What is the best continuation for Black? } 8... e6 { Black has already equalized, with massive pressure on the white pieces. From prior Lichess games with this position, Black wins 53% of the time. } *

