1. e4 { What kickstarts the Caro-Kann? } 1... c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 { What move is the Caro-Kann Exchange Variation? } 3... cxd5 4. c4 { How should you defend against the Panov Attack? } 4... Nf6 (4... dxc4 { This move, though it looks natural, gives White an early +0.5 advantage and a lead in development. Try again. }) 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Nf3 Bg4 (6... g6 { This move is good too-almost equalizing in the opening-but try to develop your light-squared bishop. }) 7. cxd5 Nxd5 (7... Qxd5??) 8. Qb3 Bxf3 (8... Nb6 { This move is good too, but there is a better move. }) 9. gxf3 e6 (9... Nb6 { This move is fine, but there is a better option that improves Black's development. }) 10. Qxb7 Nxd4 { Black has equalized from the opening! If White does not spot the hard-to-find Bb5+, forcing Black to trade the knight for the bishop, Black is already -0.3 on the tenth move of the game! } *

