1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. Bd3 { Though this move may appear as an inaccuracy, it is actually the top engine move in the position. Can you find the best continuation for Black? } 4... Nc6 5. c3 { 5.c3 is played in 75% of games in this position. What is the best move for Black here? } 5... e5 6. dxe5 Nxe5 7. Qe2 { How can you threaten a tactic here while defending your knight? } 7... Qe7! { The only move! Great job! } 8. Bb5+ { Your opponent gives a check. How should you block? } 8... Bd7 9. Bxd7+ Kxd7 10. Qb5+ Kc8 11. Qxd5?? { Your opponent blundered! How do you exploit this? } 11... Nd3+! 12. Kd1 Nxf2+! 13. Kc2 Nxh1 { Inexperienced opponents of the Caro-Kann can often blunder in the opening and early middlegame. Recognizing tactical patterns in the Caro-Kann can help you take advantage of your opponents' mistakes. } *

