{ The Caro-Kann Defense: Advance Variation is the most popular response to 2...d5, played 39% of the time. White plays 3.e5 instead of 3.exd5 cxd5, like in the Caro-Kann Defense: Exchange Variation. }
1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 { This is the Caro-Kann Defense: Advance Variation. Develop your light-squared bishop. } 3... Bf5 4. Nf3 e6 5. Bd3 Bxd3 6. Qxd3 c5 7. c3 { Black has almost equalized from the opening (+0.18). Black also has many opportunities to develop from this position. } *

