1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 { Follow the Main Line here. } 3... Bf5 4. h4 { This is the Caro-Kann Defense: Advance Variation, Tal variation. It threatens to trap the the light-squared bishop if the move e6 is ever played. It is the top line of the computer. Find a move that allows e6 to be played. } 4... h5 5. Bd3 Bxd3 6. Qxd3 Qa5+ (6... e6 { This move is perfectly fine (+0.42), but there is a slightly better move. }) 7. Nd2 e6 8. Nf3 { In the Caro-Kann: Advance, you want your knight on the f5 square... } 8... Nh6 9. O-O Nf5 10. c4 Be7 (10... Nd7 { This move is excellent too, but there is a better move. }) 11. g3 O-O { It is +0.01 from the opening, and Black has equalized. } *

