{ An example of a typical Caro-Kann Fantasy position. }
1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. f3 { 3.f3 transfers the game to the Fantasy Variation. What is the best move here? } 3... e6 4. Nc3 Bb4 5. Bd2 Ne7 (5... Nf6 { After 6.e5, White is +0.9 with a lead in development. }) 6. a3 Ba5 7. b4? Bb6 8. Be3!? e5 9. Na4 Bc7 10. Bd3 dxe4 11. Bxe4 f5 { Black is already winning (-1.2!) with massive pressure on the Black pieces. By playing e6 and calmly developing, Black equalized in the first five moves. By taking advantage of b4 and Be3, Black was able to take up space and pressure the White pieces. } *

